#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"You do not need to download these bundles yourself; the build fetches them "
"automatically (see next section)."
msgstr ""
"Man muss diese Bundles nicht selbst herunterladen; der Build holt sie "
"automatisch (siehe nächster Abschnitt)."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "The tools and how they work together"
msgstr "Die Werkzeuge und wie sie zusammenspielen"

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Tool\n"
"| Needed?\n"
"| What it does\n"
"\n"
"| **JDK 25**\n"
"| yes\n"
"| Java compiler and runtime. The code is compiled for Java 25 (`+cnf/build.bnd+`, `+gradle.properties+`).\n"
"| **Git**\n"
"| yes\n"
"| Get the source code and manage changes.\n"
"| **Gradle**\n"
"| yes, included\n"
"| The build tool: compiles, tests, checks the code style and packs the JAR. It does **not** need to be installed; the repository contains the Gradle wrapper `+./gradlew+` (Windows: `+gradlew.bat+`), which downloads the matching Gradle version (9.8.1) itself on first use.\n"
"| **bnd**\n"
"| yes, included\n"
"| The OSGi tool library. It generates the OSGi manifests and component descriptions from the `+bnd.bnd+` files and annotations, resolves which bundles are needed at runtime and builds the executable JAR from them. bnd (version 7.4.0) is loaded automatically as a Gradle plugin.\n"
"| **Bndtools**\n"
"| only with Eclipse\n"
"| An Eclipse plugin that integrates bnd into the IDE: import projects, edit `+EdgeApp.bndrun+` graphically, “Resolve” and “Run OSGi” at the push of a button, templates for new bundles.\n"
"| **Maven**\n"
"| no\n"
"| Maven is **not** used as a build tool. There is, however, the file `+cnf/pom.xml+`: it lists all third-party libraries (around 115 entries) with their version. bnd reads it and downloads the libraries from **Maven Central**, the public library server. New third-party library = entry in `+cnf/pom.xml+`. The version updates in the repository (“Bump … in /cnf”) concern this file.\n"
"| **Eclipse** or **IntelliJ IDEA**\n"
"| recommended\n"
"| IDE, see xref:development/ide/eclipse.adoc[Eclipse] and xref:development/ide/intellij.adoc[IntelliJ]. According to the xref:development/coding-guidelines.adoc[Coding Guidelines], Eclipse is the officially supported development environment.\n"
"| **Node.js/npm**, **Angular CLI**\n"
"| only for the UI\n"
"| Build and start the UI, see xref:ui/setup-ide.adoc[Setup IDE].\n"
msgstr ""
"| Werkzeug\n"
"| Nötig?\n"
"| Was es tut\n"
"\n"
"| **JDK 25**\n"
"| ja\n"
"| Java-Compiler und Laufzeit. Der Code wird für Java 25 übersetzt (`+cnf/build.bnd+`, `+gradle.properties+`).\n"
"| **Git**\n"
"| ja\n"
"| Quellcode holen und Änderungen verwalten.\n"
"| **Gradle**\n"
"| ja, kommt mit\n"
"| Das Build-Werkzeug: übersetzt, testet, prüft den Code-Stil und packt die JAR. Es muss **nicht** installiert werden; das Repository enthält den Gradle-Wrapper `+./gradlew+` (Windows: `+gradlew.bat+`), der beim ersten Aufruf die passende Gradle-Version (9.8.1) selbst herunterlädt.\n"
"| **bnd**\n"
"| ja, kommt mit\n"
"| Die OSGi-Werkzeugbibliothek. Sie erzeugt aus den `+bnd.bnd+`-Dateien und den Annotationen die OSGi-Manifeste und die Komponentenbeschreibungen, löst auf, welche Bundles zur Laufzeit nötig sind, und baut daraus die ausführbare JAR. bnd (Version 7.4.0) wird als Gradle-Plugin automatisch geladen.\n"
"| **Bndtools**\n"
"| nur mit Eclipse\n"
"| Ein Eclipse-Plugin, das bnd in die IDE einbindet: Projekte importieren, `+EdgeApp.bndrun+` grafisch bearbeiten, „Resolve“ und „Run OSGi“ per Knopf, Vorlagen für neue Bundles.\n"
"| **Maven**\n"
"| nein\n"
"| Maven wird **nicht** als Build-Werkzeug benutzt. Es gibt aber die Datei `+cnf/pom.xml+`: Sie listet alle Fremdbibliotheken (rund 115 Einträge) mit Version. bnd liest sie und lädt die Bibliotheken aus **Maven Central**, dem öffentlichen Bibliotheks-Server. Neue Fremdbibliothek = Eintrag in `+cnf/pom.xml+`. Die Versions-Updates im Repository („Bump … in /cnf“) betreffen diese Datei.\n"
"| **Eclipse** oder **IntelliJ IDEA**\n"
"| empfohlen\n"
"| IDE, siehe xref:latest@development/ide/eclipse.adoc[Eclipse] und xref:latest@development/ide/intellij.adoc[IntelliJ]. Laut xref:latest@development/coding-guidelines.adoc[Coding Guidelines] ist Eclipse die offiziell unterstützte Entwicklungsumgebung.\n"
"| **Node.js/npm**, **Angular CLI**\n"
"| nur für die UI\n"
"| Bauen und Starten der Oberfläche, siehe xref:latest@ui/setup-ide.adoc[Setup IDE].\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "From source code to the running Edge"
msgstr "Der Weg vom Quellcode zur laufenden Edge"

#. type: #sec-from-source-code-to-the-running-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Workspace settings** are in `+cnf/+`: `+build.bnd+` (Java version, default "
"libraries `+${buildpath}+`/`+${testpath}+`, library sources), `+pom.xml+` "
"(third-party libraries), `+checkstyle.xml+` (code style rules), "
"`+formatter.properties+` (Eclipse formatter)."
msgstr ""
"**Workspace-Einstellungen** stehen in `+cnf/+`: `+build.bnd+` (Java-Version, "
"Standard-Bibliotheken `+${buildpath}+`/`+${testpath}+`, Bibliotheks-"
"Quellen), `+pom.xml+` (Fremdbibliotheken), `+checkstyle.xml+` (Code-Stil-"
"Regeln), `+formatter.properties+` (Eclipse-Formatierer)."

#. type: #sec-from-source-code-to-the-running-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Each bundle** has a `+bnd.bnd+`. Under `+-buildpath+` it states which "
"other bundles and libraries the code may use. What is missing there is not "
"found by the compiler, even if it is in the repository."
msgstr ""
"**Jedes Bundle** hat eine `+bnd.bnd+`. Darin steht unter `+-buildpath+`, "
"welche anderen Bundles und Bibliotheken der Code verwenden darf. Was dort "
"fehlt, findet der Compiler nicht, auch wenn es im Repository liegt."

#. type: #sec-from-source-code-to-the-running-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Gradle** finds all directories with `+bnd.bnd+` via the bnd plugin and "
"treats them as subprojects. When building, it compiles the code; bnd "
"generates the manifest and puts the finished bundle under `+<bundle>/"
"generated/+`."
msgstr ""
"**Gradle** findet über das bnd-Plugin alle Verzeichnisse mit `+bnd.bnd+` und "
"behandelt sie als Teilprojekte. Beim Bauen übersetzt es den Code; bnd "
"erzeugt das Manifest und legt das fertige Bundle unter `+<bundle>/generated/"
"+` ab."

#. type: #sec-from-source-code-to-the-running-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**`+EdgeApp.bndrun+`** in the project `+io.openems.edge.application+` "
"describes the executable program (structure see table below)."
msgstr ""
"**`+EdgeApp.bndrun+`** im Projekt `+io.openems.edge.application+` beschreibt "
"das lauffähige Programm (Aufbau siehe Tabelle unten)."

#. type: #sec-from-source-code-to-the-running-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**`+./gradlew buildEdge+`** packs all `+-runbundles+` together with the "
"framework into an executable Fat-JAR and copies it to `+build/openems-"
"edge.jar+`."
msgstr ""
"**`+./gradlew buildEdge+`** packt alle `+-runbundles+` samt Framework in "
"eine ausführbare JAR und kopiert sie nach `+build/openems-edge.jar+`."

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Entry in `+EdgeApp.bndrun+`\n"
"| Content\n"
"\n"
"| `+-runfw+`\n"
"| the framework (Apache Felix)\n"
"| `+-runproperties+`\n"
"| start parameters: web server port 8080, configuration directory `+felix.cm.dir+`, data directory `+openems.data.dir+`\n"
"| `+-runrequires+`\n"
"| the desired bundles (around 200 entries, maintained by hand)\n"
"| `+-runbundles+`\n"
"| the complete list with all dependencies and fixed versions. It is **not written by hand**, but determined by bnd (“Resolve”).\n"
msgstr ""
"| Eintrag in `+EdgeApp.bndrun+`\n"
"| Inhalt\n"
"\n"
"| `+-runfw+`\n"
"| das Framework (Apache Felix)\n"
"| `+-runproperties+`\n"
"| Startparameter: Webserver-Port 8080, Konfigurationsverzeichnis `+felix.cm.dir+`, Datenverzeichnis `+openems.data.dir+`\n"
"| `+-runrequires+`\n"
"| die gewünschten Bundles (rund 200 Einträge, von Hand gepflegt)\n"
"| `+-runbundles+`\n"
"| die vollständige Liste mit allen Abhängigkeiten und festen Versionen. Sie wird **nicht von Hand** geschrieben, sondern von bnd ermittelt („Resolve“).\n"

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/cloud-interfaces/backend-data-transfer.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/external-interfaces/rest-control.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/external-interfaces/websocket.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/schedule/weather.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/third-party/openwb.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup"
msgstr "Einrichtung"

#. type: #sec-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"The Developer Guide describes the setup: xref:development/"
"overview.adoc[Overview], xref:development/ide/eclipse.adoc[Eclipse], "
"xref:development/ide/intellij.adoc[IntelliJ]. How to start the Edge for the "
"first time and create a first configuration is described in "
"xref:gettingstarted.adoc[Getting Started]."
msgstr ""
"Die Einrichtung beschreibt der Developer Guide: xref:latest@development/"
"overview.adoc[Overview], xref:latest@development/ide/eclipse.adoc[Eclipse], "
"xref:latest@development/ide/intellij.adoc[IntelliJ]. Den ersten Start der "
"Edge und eine erste Konfiguration zeigt "
"xref:latest@gettingstarted.adoc[Getting Started]."

#. type: #sec-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Gradle explicitly requires Java 25 for compiling via a toolchain. Gradle "
"looks for an installed JDK 25; an automatic download is not set up in the "
"repository. If only a different JDK is installed, Gradle can start with it, "
"but aborts when compiling. Several JDKs side by side are not a problem."
msgstr ""
"Gradle verlangt über eine Toolchain ausdrücklich Java 25 zum Übersetzen. "
"Gradle sucht dafür ein installiertes JDK 25; ein automatischer Download ist "
"im Repository nicht eingerichtet. Ist nur ein anderes JDK installiert, kann "
"Gradle damit zwar starten, bricht beim Übersetzen aber ab. Mehrere JDKs "
"nebeneinander sind kein Problem."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "How the Edge is configured"
msgstr "Wie die Edge konfiguriert wird"

#. type: #sec-how-the-edge-is-configured
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"The Edge has **no** configuration file in the sense of "
"`+application.properties+`. Everything that makes up a system (which "
"devices, which addresses, which control algorithms) is a list of **component "
"configurations** in the Configuration Admin. The ways of changing it are "
"described in xref:edge/configuration.adoc[Configuration]."
msgstr ""
"Die Edge hat **keine** Konfigurationsdatei im Sinne von "
"`+application.properties+`. Alles, was eine Anlage ausmacht (welche Geräte, "
"welche Adressen, welche Regelungen), ist eine Liste von **Komponenten-"
"Konfigurationen** im Configuration Admin. Die Wege, sie zu ändern, "
"beschreibt xref:latest@edge/configuration.adoc[Configuration]."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Structure of a configuration"
msgstr "Aufbau einer Konfiguration"

#. type: #sec-structure-of-a-configuration
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Each Factory has a **Factory-PID**, e.g. `+Meter.Janitza.UMG96RME+` or "
"`+Controller.Debug.Log+`. In the code it is in `+@Component(name = …)+`."
msgstr ""
"Jede Komponentenart hat eine **Factory-PID**, z. B. "
"`+Meter.Janitza.UMG96RME+` oder `+Controller.Debug.Log+`. Sie steht im Code "
"in `+@Component(name = …)+`."

#. type: #sec-structure-of-a-configuration
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"An Instance has a **Component-ID** (field `+id+`, e.g. `+meter0+`) and "
"further fields from the respective `+Config+` class (e.g. `+modbus.id+`, "
"`+modbusUnitId+`, `+type+`)."
msgstr ""
"Eine konkrete Instanz hat eine **Komponenten-ID** (Feld `+id+`, z. B. "
"`+meter0+`) und weitere Felder aus der jeweiligen `+Config+`-Klasse (z. B. "
"`+modbus.id+`, `+modbusUnitId+`, `+type+`)."

#. type: #sec-structure-of-a-configuration
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Components refer to each other via IDs: the meter names its Modbus Bridge "
"(`+modbus.id=modbus0+`), the Controller its ESS and meter."
msgstr ""
"Komponenten verweisen über IDs aufeinander: Der Zähler nennt seine Modbus-"
"Bridge (`+modbus.id=modbus0+`), der Controller seinen Speicher und Zähler."

#. type: #sec-structure-of-a-configuration
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Some core components exist exactly once, with a fixed ID: `+_cycle+` (cycle "
"time), `+_power+` (ESS Power), `+_meta+`, `+_sum+` etc."
msgstr ""
"Einige Kernkomponenten gibt es genau einmal, mit fester ID: `+_cycle+` "
"(Zykluszeit), `+_power+` (Leistungsverteilung), `+_meta+`, `+_sum+` usw."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where the configuration is stored"
msgstr "Wo die Konfiguration gespeichert wird"

#. type: #sec-where-the-configuration-is-stored
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"The Configuration Admin stores each configuration as a text file in the "
"directory `+felix.cm.dir+`. The dots of the PID become subfolders (e.g. "
"`+org/apache/felix/http.config+` for the PID `+org.apache.felix.http+`); "
"values are stored as `+key=\"value\"+`, with a type identifier for non-text "
"values. This behavior comes from Apache Felix and is not specific to OpenEMS."
msgstr ""
"Der Configuration Admin legt jede Konfiguration als Textdatei im Verzeichnis "
"`+felix.cm.dir+` ab. Die Punkte der PID werden dabei zu Unterordnern (z. B. "
"`+org/apache/felix/http.config+` für die PID `+org.apache.felix.http+`); "
"Werte stehen als `+schlüssel=\"wert\"+`, mit Typkennung bei Nicht-Text-"
"Werten. Dieses Verhalten ist das von Apache Felix, nicht OpenEMS-spezifisch."

#. type: #sec-where-the-configuration-is-stored
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Default according to `+EdgeApp.bndrun+`: `+c:/openems/config+`. On macOS/"
"Linux this creates a folder named `+c:+` in the working directory (for "
"`+io.openems.edge.application+` it is in `+.gitignore+`). It is better to "
"set `+-Dfelix.cm.dir=…+` at startup."
msgstr ""
"Standard laut `+EdgeApp.bndrun+`: `+c:/openems/config+`. Unter macOS/Linux "
"entsteht daraus ein Ordner namens `+c:+` im Arbeitsverzeichnis (für "
"`+io.openems.edge.application+` steht er in `+.gitignore+`). Besser beim "
"Start `+-Dfelix.cm.dir=…+` setzen."

#. type: #sec-where-the-configuration-is-stored
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"On a device following xref:edge/deploy/systemd.adoc[Deploy on Debian/"
"Ubuntu]: `+/etc/openems.d+`, JAR in `+/usr/lib/openems+`."
msgstr ""
"Auf einem Gerät nach xref:latest@edge/deploy/systemd.adoc[Deploy on Debian/"
"Ubuntu]: `+/etc/openems.d+`, JAR in `+/usr/lib/openems+`."

#. type: #sec-where-the-configuration-is-stored
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Data of the components (e.g. the local rrd4j history) is stored under "
"`+openems.data.dir+`."
msgstr ""
"Daten der Komponenten (z. B. die lokale Historie rrd4j) liegen unter "
"`+openems.data.dir+`."

#. type: #sec-where-the-configuration-is-stored
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"For an empty test environment, it is enough to delete the folder before "
"starting."
msgstr ""
"Für eine leere Testumgebung genügt es, den Ordner vor dem Start zu löschen."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Creating a new bundle"
msgstr "Ein neues Bundle anlegen"

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "With Bndtools templates"
msgstr "Mit Bndtools-Vorlagen"

#. type: #sec-with-bndtools-templates
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"OpenEMS provides project templates for Bndtools (defined in "
"`+io.openems.common/bnd.bnd+`, files under `+io.openems.common/resources/"
"templates+`):"
msgstr ""
"OpenEMS liefert Projektvorlagen für Bndtools (definiert in "
"`+io.openems.common/bnd.bnd+`, Dateien unter `+io.openems.common/resources/"
"templates+`):"

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Template\n"
"| Result\n"
"\n"
"| OpenEMS Controller\n"
"| Controller with `+Config+`, `+…Impl+`, test\n"
"| OpenEMS Device\n"
"| device without a specific protocol\n"
"| OpenEMS Modbus Device\n"
"| device with Modbus connection\n"
"| OpenEMS Api\n"
"| API bundle with its own Nature\n"
msgstr ""
"| Vorlage\n"
"| Ergebnis\n"
"\n"
"| OpenEMS Controller\n"
"| Controller mit `+Config+`, `+…Impl+`, Test\n"
"| OpenEMS Device\n"
"| Gerät ohne bestimmtes Protokoll\n"
"| OpenEMS Modbus Device\n"
"| Gerät mit Modbus-Anbindung\n"
"| OpenEMS Api\n"
"| API-Bundle mit eigener Nature\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"xref:edge/implement.adoc[Implementing a Device] shows the steps in Eclipse. "
"Without Eclipse, the easiest way is to copy a similar existing bundle and "
"rename the package, classes and Factory-PID."
msgstr ""
"xref:latest@edge/implement.adoc[Implementing a Device] zeigt die Schritte in "
"Eclipse. Ohne Eclipse kopiert man am einfachsten ein ähnliches bestehendes "
"Bundle und benennt Paket, Klassen und Factory-PID um."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adding the bundle to the Edge"
msgstr "Bundle in die Edge aufnehmen"

#. type: #sec-adding-the-bundle-to-the-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid "A new bundle is built, but is **not yet** part of the Edge. To add it:"
msgstr ""
"Ein neues Bundle wird gebaut, ist aber noch **nicht** in der Edge enthalten. "
"Dafür:"

#. type: #sec-adding-the-bundle-to-the-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Enter it in `+EdgeApp.bndrun+` under `+-runrequires+` "
"(`+bnd.identity;id='io.openems.edge.…'+`). In Bndtools: drag the bundle from "
"the __Repositories__ list to __Run Requirements__ and save."
msgstr ""
"In `+EdgeApp.bndrun+` unter `+-runrequires+` eintragen "
"(`+bnd.identity;id='io.openems.edge.…'+`). In Bndtools: Bundle aus der Liste "
"__Repositories__ in __Run Requirements__ ziehen und speichern."

#. type: #sec-adding-the-bundle-to-the-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"Run **Resolve** so that bnd recalculates the list `+-runbundles+`: in "
"Bndtools with the __Resolve__ button (adopt the result with __Update__), on "
"the command line with `+./"
"gradlew :io.openems.edge.application:resolve.EdgeApp+`."
msgstr ""
"**Resolve** ausführen, damit bnd die Liste `+-runbundles+` neu berechnet: in "
"Bndtools mit dem Knopf __Resolve__ (Ergebnis mit __Update__ übernehmen), auf "
"der Kommandozeile mit `+./"
"gradlew :io.openems.edge.application:resolve.EdgeApp+`."

#. type: #sec-adding-the-bundle-to-the-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid "Commit both changes to `+EdgeApp.bndrun+`."
msgstr "Beide Änderungen der `+EdgeApp.bndrun+` mit einchecken."

#. type: #sec-adding-the-bundle-to-the-edge
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"If a bundle is only entered in `+-runrequires+` and not resolved, it is "
"missing from the JAR. If Resolve reports an error, a dependency is usually "
"missing: a package that no bundle exports, or a third-party library that is "
"not in `+cnf/pom.xml+`."
msgstr ""
"Wird ein Bundle nur in `+-runrequires+` eingetragen und nicht aufgelöst, "
"fehlt es in der JAR. Meldet Resolve einen Fehler, fehlt meist eine "
"Abhängigkeit: ein Paket, das kein Bundle exportiert, oder eine "
"Fremdbibliothek, die nicht in `+cnf/pom.xml+` steht."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Typical pitfalls"
msgstr "Typische Stolpersteine"

#. type: #sec-typical-pitfalls
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Class not found when compiling**, even though it is in the repository: the "
"bundle is missing from the `+-buildpath+` of your own `+bnd.bnd+`."
msgstr ""
"**Klasse nicht gefunden beim Übersetzen**, obwohl sie im Repository liegt: "
"Das Bundle fehlt im `+-buildpath+` der eigenen `+bnd.bnd+`."

#. type: #sec-typical-pitfalls
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Package not found at runtime**: the other bundle does not export the "
"package. In OpenEMS, packages are usually exported via `+package-info.java+` "
"with `+@org.osgi.annotation.versioning.Version+` and `+@Export+`."
msgstr ""
"**Paket zur Laufzeit nicht gefunden**: Das andere Bundle exportiert das "
"Paket nicht. In OpenEMS werden Pakete meist über `+package-info.java+` mit "
"`+@org.osgi.annotation.versioning.Version+` und `+@Export+` exportiert."

#. type: #sec-typical-pitfalls
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Component does not start**, even though it is configured: a mandatory "
"reference (`+@Reference+` with `+MANDATORY+`) is not satisfied, e.g. wrong "
"ID in `+ess.id+`. In the Apache Felix Web Console under __OSGi → "
"Components__ you can see which reference is missing."
msgstr ""
"**Komponente startet nicht**, obwohl konfiguriert: Eine Pflicht-Referenz "
"(`+@Reference+` mit `+MANDATORY+`) ist nicht erfüllt, z. B. falsche ID in "
"`+ess.id+`. In der Felix-Webkonsole unter __OSGi → Components__ sieht man, "
"welche Referenz fehlt."

#. type: #sec-typical-pitfalls
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**New component missing in the Apache Felix Web Console**: bundle not "
"entered in `+EdgeApp.bndrun+` or not resolved again."
msgstr ""
"**Neue Komponente fehlt in der Webkonsole**: Bundle nicht in "
"`+EdgeApp.bndrun+` eingetragen oder nicht neu aufgelöst."

#. type: #sec-typical-pitfalls
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Gradle aborts with a toolchain error**: JDK 25 is missing (see <<sec-"
"setup,Setup>>)."
msgstr ""
"**Gradle bricht mit Toolchain-Fehler ab**: JDK 25 fehlt (siehe <<sec-"
"setup,Einrichtung>>)."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Eclipse after a git pull"
msgstr "Eclipse nach einem git pull"

#. type: #sec-eclipse-after-a-git-pull
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"A `+git pull+` changes the folders in the repository, but not the project "
"list in Eclipse. Bundles that are added or removed must be updated in "
"Eclipse by hand."
msgstr ""
"Ein `+git pull+` ändert die Ordner im Repository, aber nicht die "
"Projektliste in Eclipse. Bundles, die neu hinzukommen oder entfernt werden, "
"muss man in Eclipse von Hand nachziehen."

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Message in Eclipse\n"
"| Cause\n"
"| Remedy\n"
"\n"
"| “Project 'io.openems.edge.core' is missing required Java project: 'io.openems.common.tariff.api'”, followed by hundreds of consequential errors (“… cannot be resolved to a type”, also for `+org.osgi+` and `+org.junit+`)\n"
"| A bundle from the `+-buildpath+` is in the repository, but not imported into Eclipse.\n"
"| __File → Import → General → Existing Projects into Workspace__, select the repository as root, tick all projects that are not grayed out, do **not** tick “Copy projects into workspace”.\n"
"| “The project does not have a bnd.bnd file” and almost everywhere “The container 'Bnd Bundle Path' references non existing library '…/generated/….jar'”\n"
"| Eclipse still has a project whose `+bnd.bnd+` no longer exists (e.g. a removed bundle whose `+bin+` and `+generated+` folders were left behind). In one observed case, Bndtools built no JARs while it was in the workspace, not even for `+io.openems.wrapper+` and `+io.openems.common+`.\n"
"| Delete the project in Eclipse (right-click → __Delete__, do **not** tick “Delete project contents on disk”). In that case, the workspace built again afterwards.\n"
msgstr ""
"| Meldung in Eclipse\n"
"| Ursache\n"
"| Abhilfe\n"
"\n"
"| „Project 'io.openems.edge.core' is missing required Java project: 'io.openems.common.tariff.api'“, danach hunderte Folgefehler („… cannot be resolved to a type“, auch für `+org.osgi+` und `+org.junit+`)\n"
"| Ein Bundle aus dem `+-buildpath+` liegt im Repository, ist aber nicht in Eclipse importiert.\n"
"| __File → Import → General → Existing Projects into Workspace__, als Wurzel das Repository wählen, alle nicht ausgegrauten Projekte anhaken, „Copy projects into workspace“ **nicht** anhaken.\n"
"| „The project does not have a bnd.bnd file“ und fast überall „The container 'Bnd Bundle Path' references non existing library '…/generated/….jar'“\n"
"| In Eclipse ist noch ein Projekt, dessen `+bnd.bnd+` nicht mehr existiert (z. B. ein entferntes Bundle, dessen `+bin+`- und `+generated+`-Ordner liegen geblieben sind). In einem beobachteten Fall baute Bndtools keine JARs, solange es im Workspace war, nicht einmal für `+io.openems.wrapper+` und `+io.openems.common+`.\n"
"| Projekt in Eclipse löschen (Rechtsklick → __Delete__, „Delete project contents on disk“ **nicht** anhaken). In diesem Fall baute der Workspace danach wieder.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"To check: every folder with `+bnd.bnd+` in the repository must exist as a "
"project in Eclipse, plus `+cnf+`. Conversely, every Eclipse project except "
"`+cnf+` needs a `+bnd.bnd+`."
msgstr ""
"Zur Kontrolle: Jeder Ordner mit `+bnd.bnd+` im Repository muss als Projekt "
"in Eclipse vorhanden sein, dazu `+cnf+`. Umgekehrt braucht jedes Eclipse-"
"Projekt außer `+cnf+` eine `+bnd.bnd+`."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid "Further notes:"
msgstr "Weitere Hinweise:"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Do not build with Gradle and Eclipse at the same time.** Both write to the "
"same `+generated/+` folders. If you call `+./gradlew+` in between, select "
"all projects in Eclipse afterwards and refresh them with F5."
msgstr ""
"**Gradle und Eclipse nicht gleichzeitig bauen lassen.** Beide schreiben in "
"dieselben `+generated/+`-Ordner. Wer zwischendurch `+./gradlew+` aufruft, "
"sollte danach in Eclipse alle Projekte markieren und mit F5 neu einlesen."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Wait after “Clean all”.** Clean deletes all generated JARs. While around "
"250 projects are rebuilt, the Problems view temporarily shows many errors. "
"Only evaluate them after the build has finished (__Window → Show View → "
"Progress__)."
msgstr ""
"**Nach „Clean all“ abwarten.** Clean löscht alle erzeugten JARs. Während "
"rund 250 Projekte neu gebaut werden, zeigt die Problems-Ansicht "
"vorübergehend viele Fehler. Erst nach Ende des Builds auswerten (__Window → "
"Show View → Progress__)."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"**Reading the error list:** The entries of type “Build Path Problem” and "
"“Bndtools …” are important. The many “cannot be resolved” errors are almost "
"always consequential errors."
msgstr ""
"**Fehlerliste lesen:** Wichtig sind die Einträge vom Typ „Build Path "
"Problem“ und „Bndtools …“. Die vielen „cannot be resolved“-Fehler sind fast "
"immer Folgefehler."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read on"
msgstr "Weiter lesen"

#. type: #sec-read-on
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"xref:development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc[Cycle, Scheduler and "
"ESS Power]: what happens every second"
msgstr ""
"xref:development/fundamentals/cycle-and-ess-power.adoc[Zyklus]: was jede "
"Sekunde passiert"

#. type: #sec-read-on
#: modules/ROOT/pages/development/fundamentals/osgi-and-tools.adoc
msgid ""
"xref:edge/implement.adoc[Implementing a Device]: step-by-step example with a "
"simulated meter"
msgstr ""
"xref:latest@edge/implement.adoc[Implementing a Device]: Schritt-für-Schritt-"
"Beispiel mit einem simulierten Zähler"
